# Dashboard Design Constraints

Hard constraints for rendering the self-contained meeting dashboard in `meeting-visualizer` Step 5.

## 1. Self-Containment

- Single HTML5 file. All CSS in one `<style>` block. All JavaScript in one `<script>` block.
- Zero external requests: no fonts, no CDNs, no images, no network calls.
- All state toggles implemented inline; no framework dependencies.

## 2. Visual System

- Neutral background (`#f8f8f6`), high-contrast text (`#1a1a1a`), one accent color reserved for decisions.
- System font stack only: `-apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif`.
- Max content width `960px`, centered. Minimum readable font size `14px`.

## 3. Layout Rules

- Layout follows the archetype table in `references/meeting-types.md`.
- Four universal sections always present: Decisions, Action Items, Open Questions, Verbatim Quotes.
- Action items render as checkboxes with owner and due date; never as free text lists.
- Verbatim quotes render in quotation marks with the speaker attribution and a positional transcript marker.

## 4. Content Fidelity

- Quotes are unedited transcript excerpts. Never paraphrase inside quotation marks.
- Unconfirmed facts carry the label `Unconfirmed`.
- Decisions show rationale; a decision without rationale renders as `No rationale recorded`.

## 5. Security

- All transcript-derived text escapes HTML entities before injection.
- No user-supplied HTML, JavaScript, or URLs are executed.